# Test: the commit refuses a plugin external name the connect-back refuses.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-doctor-coverage-12-plugin-infra AC-23 -- `plugin external a_b`
#            is refused by `ze config validate` and by `ze start`, naming the
#            name and the allowed form, from the one declaration
#            (ipc.pluginNamePattern, internal/component/plugin/ipc/plugin_name.go)
#            the auth handshake reads.
# PREVENTS:  plan/journal/validate-accepts-what-start-refuses.md, 2026-11-10:
#            the name validated, the daemon started, and the plugin hung for its
#            connect-back timeout because AuthenticateWithLookup refused it.
#
# The enforcing producer is ExternalPluginNameValidator
# (internal/component/config/validators.go), reached through the ze:validate
# on plugin/external/name in ze-plugin-conf.yang, walked by
# ValidateCustomSections. Revert the ze:validate and both commands accept the
# config: validate exits 0 and the daemon starts.
#
# The bgp block routes the config to runYANGConfig rather than the hub-only
# parser (see test/parse/config-startup-refuses-invalid-validator.ci).

tmpfs=bad-name.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external a_b {
		run "/bin/true"
	}
}

bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote { ip 127.0.0.1; }
			local { ip 127.0.0.1; accept false; }
		}
		session {
			asn { local 65000; remote 65001; }
			router-id 1.2.3.4;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate bad-name.conf:exit=1
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=a_b
expect=stdout:contains=letters, digits and hyphens

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze start bad-name.conf:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=config validation failed
expect=stderr:contains=a_b
expect=stderr:contains=letters, digits and hyphens
